# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# M8 external validation -- ORCA STEOM-CCSD reference for the GANSU comparison.
#
# Run one job per molecule. Match GANSU: cc-pVDZ, RI (RIJCOSX + cc-pVDZ/C for
# the CC part), frozen core (ORCA default), 5 roots, closed-shell singlets.
# Keep the geometry file IDENTICAL to GANSU's xyz (../xyz/<Molecule>.xyz).
#
# ORCA has STEOM-CCSD; it has NO ADC(2). For the ADC(2) column use PySCF+adcc
# (adcc.adc2), Turbomole (ricc2 adc(2)), or Q-Chem -- same cc-pVDZ, frozen core.
#
# Report the vertical excitation energies in eV (ORCA prints them in the
# "STEOM-CCSD RESULTS" / "TRANSITION ELECTRIC DIPOLE MOMENTS" block).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ==== Formaldehyde ====
! STEOM-CCSD cc-pVDZ RIJCOSX cc-pVDZ/C cc-pVDZ/J TightSCF
%mdci
  nroots 5
  dorootwise true
end
* xyzfile 0 1 Formaldehyde.xyz

# ==== Ethylene (C2H4) : copy the block above, change the geometry line to ====
# * xyzfile 0 1 C2H4.xyz

# ==== Water (H2O) : ====
# * xyzfile 0 1 H2O.xyz
#
# Note: H2O's low singlets are Rydberg; cc-pVDZ has no diffuse functions, so
# the ABSOLUTE energies are not physical -- but GANSU and ORCA use the same
# basis, so the code-vs-code AGREEMENT is still the quantity being validated.
